# The bat: a creature of the Mists (WLD-56; Sitting E §§ 6–7). Ruled by Darko 2026-10-15 12:09 (D4).
kind: bat
name: a bat
voice: a small dark flicker in the fog, there and gone and there again
about: a bat out of the Mists; it flits and chitters, and a voice too close sends it away
what: >
  A bat that came out of the Mists with the season. It is skittish, and it is more sound than shape:
  a flicker past your head, a chitter too high to quite hear. Speak right beside it, or frighten it,
  and it jinks away into the Mists.
ring_m: 30
moods:
  fear: 0..3 = 2 | settled | flighty | skittish | panicked
  curiosity: 0..3 = 1 | elsewhere | aware of you | circling | all around you
  hunger: 0..3 = 1 | fed | peckish | hungry | starving

reaction flit "it flits past": when true says A bat flits past {actor}'s head, there and gone and back again.
reaction chitter "it chitters in the fog": when not act.approaching says Something small chitters in the fog near {actor}, too high to quite hear.
reaction loop "it loops round you": when self.curiosity >= 2 says The bat loops twice around {actor}, close enough to feel the air move.
reaction flee "it jinks away into the Mists": when self.fear >= 3 or (act.verb == "say" and act.distance_m < 10) does flee says The bat jinks away into the Mists.
